  "label": "Modal grounding union elimination rule under the #477 loop: actual reflexivity, no contingent…",
  "legacy_id": "CONFIG-MODAL-GROUNDING-UNION",
  "description": "Modal grounding union elimination rule (#542) under the #477 loop: actual reflexivity, no contingent ground of a necessary bearer and a well-founded cross-world union of necessary-to-necessary support, with a necessary bearer and explicit excluded middle, yield a necessarily underived bearer; edge invariance is not needed. Selections drop each union-route premise against the registered finite controls (rotating cross-world cycle, switching contingent ground, varying edges). Certified witnesses outside this finite-model registry: PARITY-UNION-REGRESS (Nat carrier: two locally depth-one worlds whose cycle-free union has an infinite descending regress) and FINITE-NECESSARY-UNION-CLASSIFICATION (classical, so outside this zero-axiom profile). Configurations are inputs; statuses are computed only from live certificates. No premise is established and no root premise closes. #950 adds an explicitly OPEN equivalent common-rank presentation via an arbitrary WF codomain. It is not a defense or a weaker premise. The three new configuration bridge certificates remain zero-axiom; the separate parity comparison uses the approved Mathlib axiom set.",
  "seed_statement_id": "d236f537-dd57-50ec-9676-cee87b19242a",
